# File: tests/bdd/features/reduce_to_budget.feature
# Generated from: specs/139-add-a-reduce-to-budget-step-that-bakes-a-generated-high-poly-asset-onto-an-in-budget-mesh/requirements.md
Feature: Reduce a generated high-poly asset to its Desktop budget

  @SCN001
  Scenario: An over-budget asset is reduced into budget with its originals kept
    Given an unrigged multi-part asset above its Desktop triangle budget
    When the reduce step runs
    Then each part keeps its name, transform, origin, and parent
    And the triangle total is at or below the resolved Desktop budget
    And the originals sit in the hidden <Name>_High collection, which finalize never reads

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The budget is split by surface area
    Given parts with different surface areas and no overrides
    When the budget is planned
    Then each part's target is proportional to its area and at least 12 triangles

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Per-part overrides win and invalid overrides are refused
    Given overrides for some parts
    When the budget is planned
    Then the overridden parts use their values and the rest share the remainder by area
    And overrides above the budget fail with reduce.overrides_exceed_budget before any change

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The reduced asset carries one atlas and one baked texture set
    Given a completed reduce run
    Then every reduced mesh has one UVMap with no overlap inside 0 to 1
    And M_<Name>_Body uses T_<Name>_Body_BC, _N, and _ORM at the Desktop texture size

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Cage and ray distance are configurable per part
    Given an asset-wide cage and a per-part ray distance
    When the reduce step runs
    Then each part reports the cage extrusion and ray distance it used

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Ray misses are reported and fail above the threshold
    Given a part whose unbaked share exceeds the miss threshold
    When the reduce step runs
    Then it fails with reduce.bake_misses naming the part, its share, and its settings
    And the scene is unchanged

  @SCN007
  Scenario: The reduced asset passes finalize
    Given a reduced standard_prop and a reduced environment_piece
    When finalize runs validate through reimport
    Then both pass, and the atlas layout is kept

  @SCN008
  Scenario: A rerun rebuilds from <Name>_High
    Given an asset that was already reduced
    When the reduce step runs again with different settings
    Then <Name> is rebuilt from <Name>_High, which is neither modified nor duplicated

  @SCN009
  Scenario: An asset already in budget is left alone
    Given an asset within its Desktop budget and no <Name>_High
    When the reduce step runs
    Then the result state is within_budget and the scene is unchanged

  @SCN010
  Scenario: A rigged asset or the terrain class is refused
    Given an asset with an armature, or a request for class terrain
    When the reduce step runs
    Then it fails with reduce.rigged or reduce.class_unsupported and the scene is unchanged

  @SCN011
  Scenario: The MCP job loads the result back only into an unchanged session
    Given a reduce_asset job started on the open session
    When the background run finishes and the session's <Name> is unchanged
    Then <Name> and <Name>_High are loaded back
    But when the session changed, the job fails with reduce.session_changed and the result .blend path

  @SCN012
  Scenario: All entry points share one implementation and result shape
    Given the panel operator, run_for_mcp, the CLI reduce command, and the reduce_asset tool
    When each runs the same request
    Then each returns the same result fields
